# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On a real quantum processor, noise turns the pure state $|\\psi\\rangle$ that a circuit is designed to prepare into a mixed state $\\rho$. Full quantum state tomography can reconstruct $\\rho$, but the number of measurements it needs grows exponentially with the number of qubits. Votto et al. [\\[1\\]](#references) instead learned a compact model of $\\rho$ for up to 96 qubits from randomized measurements. This tutorial follows their workflow.\n"
msgstr "Pada pemproses kuantum sebenar, noise menukarkan keadaan tulen $|\\psi\\rangle$ yang litar direka untuk disediakan kepada keadaan bercampur $\\rho$. Tomografi keadaan kuantum penuh boleh membina semula $\\rho$, tetapi bilangan pengukuran yang diperlukannya bertambah secara eksponen dengan bilangan qubit. Votto et al. [\\[1\\]](#references) sebaliknya mempelajari model padat bagi $\\rho$ sehingga 96 qubit daripada pengukuran rawak. Tutorial ini mengikuti aliran kerja mereka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a randomized measurement [\\[2\\]](#references), every qubit $i$ is rotated by an independent random unitary $u_i$ and then measured in the computational basis. One draw of the rotations is called a *measurement setting*, and each setting is repeated for $N_M$ shots. A shot with outcome bits $s_i$ gives the *classical shadow* [\\[3\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr "Dalam pengukuran rawak [\\[2\\]](#references), setiap qubit $i$ diputar oleh unitari rawak bebas $u_i$ dan kemudian diukur dalam asas pengiraan. Satu cabutan putaran dipanggil *tetapan pengukuran*, dan setiap tetapan diulang untuk $N_M$ tembakan. Tembakan dengan bit hasil $s_i$ memberikan *bayang klasik* [\\[3\\]](#references)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat\\rho=\\bigotimes_{i=1}^{N}\\left(3\\,u_i^\\dagger|s_i\\rangle\\langle s_i|u_i-\\mathbb{1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat\\rho=\\bigotimes_{i=1}^{N}\\left(3\\,u_i^\\dagger|s_i\\rangle\\langle s_i|u_i-\\mathbb{1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "whose average over settings and shots is $\\rho$. The prerequisite tutorial draws each $u_i$ from the three Pauli bases; this tutorial, like the paper, draws them uniformly from all single-qubit unitaries (Haar random), and the same formula applies.\n"
msgstr "yang purata ke atas tetapan dan tembakan ialah $\\rho$. Tutorial prasyarat mencabut setiap $u_i$ daripada tiga asas Pauli; tutorial ini, seperti kertas kajian itu, mencabutnya secara seragam daripada semua unitari qubit tunggal (rawak Haar), dan formula yang sama terpakai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shadows estimate properties of a few qubits at a time. The paper combines them into a *matrix product operator* (MPO), which writes the density matrix as a chain of small tensors, one per qubit; noisy states with short-range correlations need only small bonds between neighboring tensors. Like the density matrix renormalization group (DMRG) algorithm, the learner sweeps along the chain and updates one tensor at a time, so that the model matches the shadows on the window of $2\\ell+1$ qubits centered on that tensor (Equation 4 of the paper). The bond dimension stays fixed during these updates, so the learner never truncates the model. Because data enter only through these windows, the number of settings needed does not grow with the length of the chain.\n"
msgstr "Bayang menganggar sifat beberapa qubit pada satu masa. Kertas kajian itu menggabungkannya menjadi *operator hasil darab matriks* (MPO), yang menulis matriks ketumpatan sebagai rantaian tensor kecil, satu bagi setiap qubit; keadaan bernoise dengan korelasi jarak pendek hanya memerlukan ikatan kecil antara tensor bersebelahan. Seperti algoritma kumpulan penormalan semula matriks ketumpatan (DMRG), pembelajar menyapu sepanjang rantaian dan mengemas kini satu tensor pada satu masa, supaya model sepadan dengan bayang pada tetingkap $2\\ell+1$ qubit yang berpusat pada tensor itu (Persamaan 4 dalam kertas kajian). Dimensi ikatan kekal tetap semasa kemas kini ini, jadi pembelajar tidak pernah memangkas model. Oleh sebab data hanya masuk melalui tetingkap ini, bilangan tetapan yang diperlukan tidak bertambah dengan panjang rantaian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The settings are split into a training set and a testing set. On the testing set, the paper estimates the max fidelity between $\\rho$ and the model $\\sigma$,\n"
msgstr "Tetapan dibahagikan kepada set latihan dan set ujian. Pada set ujian, kertas kajian itu menganggar kesetiaan maksimum antara $\\rho$ dan model $\\sigma$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}(\\rho,\\sigma)=\\frac{\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)}{\\max\\left(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2,\\ \\mathrm{tr}\\,\\sigma^2\\right)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}(\\rho,\\sigma)=\\frac{\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)}{\\max\\left(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2,\\ \\mathrm{tr}\\,\\sigma^2\\right)}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ directly would take exponentially many measurements. Instead, the paper assumes the *approximate factorization condition* (AFC): correlations in $\\rho$ decay within a few qubits, so global overlaps and purities factor into terms on blocks of $k$ neighboring qubits. The purity also gives the Rényi-2 entropy $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2$, which measures how mixed the state is.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ secara langsung memerlukan pengukuran yang banyaknya eksponen. Sebaliknya, kertas kajian itu mengandaikan *syarat pemfaktoran hampir* (AFC): korelasi dalam $\\rho$ susut dalam beberapa qubit, jadi pertindihan dan ketulenan global difaktorkan kepada sebutan pada blok $k$ qubit bersebelahan. Ketulenan juga memberikan entropi Rényi-2 $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2$, yang mengukur sejauh mana keadaan itu bercampur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The paper prepares the depth-$D$ kicked-Ising state\n"
msgstr "Kertas kajian itu menyediakan keadaan Ising bertendang berkedalaman $D$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle=\\left(\\prod_{j} e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}\\prod_j e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X_j}\\right)^{D}|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle=\\left(\\prod_{j} e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}\\prod_j e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X_j}\\right)^{D}|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "on 96 qubits of `ibm_brisbane`, an Eagle processor, with 2,048 settings of 1,024 shots for $D=1$. Figure 1(c,d) of the paper reports two results for $D=1$:\n"
msgstr "pada 96 qubit `ibm_brisbane`, pemproses Eagle, dengan 2,048 tetapan 1,024 tembakan untuk $D=1$. Rajah 1(c,d) kertas kajian itu melaporkan dua hasil untuk $D=1$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learned model reaches $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}\\approx 75\\%$ with the experimental state at $N=96$, far above the overlap of the ideal state $|\\psi\\rangle$ with the experiment.\n"
msgstr "Model yang dipelajari mencapai $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}\\approx 75\\%$ dengan keadaan eksperimen pada $N=96$, jauh melebihi pertindihan keadaan unggul $|\\psi\\rangle$ dengan eksperimen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entropy grows linearly, $S_2\\approx(0.14\\text{ to }0.15)\\,N$, and the entropy of the model agrees with an independent estimate from the testing set.\n"
msgstr "Entropi bertambah secara linear, $S_2\\approx(0.14\\text{ hingga }0.15)\\,N$, dan entropi model sepadan dengan anggaran bebas daripada set ujian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial checks both results, first in an eight-qubit simulation where the exact answers are known, and then in a new 96-qubit run on `ibm_fez`, a Heron r2 processor. The learner is an independent Julia implementation of the equations in the paper and its supplement.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menyemak kedua-dua hasil, pertama dalam simulasi lapan qubit di mana jawapan tepat diketahui, dan kemudian dalam larian 96 qubit baharu pada `ibm_fez`, pemproses Heron r2. Pembelajar ialah pelaksanaan Julia bebas bagi persamaan dalam kertas kajian dan suplemennya.\n"

