#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The helper module [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), which the Setup cell downloads, implements the learner. The tutorial calls the following functions from it:\n"
msgstr "Modul pembantu [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), yang dimuat turun oleh sel Persediaan, melaksanakan pembelajar. Tutorial ini memanggil fungsi berikut daripadanya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Function | Purpose |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | Exact MPO of the ideal kicked-Ising state, or of the state after local depolarizing noise |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Randomly assign measurement settings to training and testing sets (half each by default) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Shadow estimates of every learning window, from the training settings only |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior for common randomized measurements (CRM), fitted to the measured purity of each window, as in the paper |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Sweep the one-site update of the paper along the chain, starting from the maximally mixed state |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | Exact $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ between two MPOs |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | AFC estimates of $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ from the testing settings, with jackknife error bars |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Fungsi | Tujuan |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | MPO tepat bagi keadaan Ising bertendang unggul, atau bagi keadaan selepas noise penyahkutuban setempat |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Menetapkan tetapan pengukuran secara rawak kepada set latihan dan ujian (separuh setiap satu secara lalai) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Anggaran bayang bagi setiap tetingkap pembelajaran, daripada tetapan latihan sahaja |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior untuk pengukuran rawak biasa (CRM), dipadankan dengan ketulenan terukur bagi setiap tetingkap, seperti dalam kertas kajian |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Menyapu kemas kini satu tapak daripada kertas kajian sepanjang rantaian, bermula daripada keadaan bercampur maksimum |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ dan $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ tepat antara dua MPO |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | Anggaran AFC bagi $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ dan $S_2$ daripada tetapan ujian, dengan bar ralat jackknife |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learner stores the MPO in the Pauli basis. This keeps the model Hermitian with unit trace, but it does not force the model to be positive semidefinite, so the notebook reports how negative its eigenvalues become.\n"
msgstr "Pembelajar menyimpan MPO dalam asas Pauli. Ini mengekalkan model Hermitian dengan surih unit, tetapi tidak memaksa model menjadi separa tentu positif, jadi buku nota melaporkan sejauh mana nilai eigennya menjadi negatif.\n"

