# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The residual measures how far the model's windows are from the training shadows. It drops when the one-site updates start, in the second sweep, and then stays approximately constant instead of reaching zero, because the shadows contain statistical noise that a model with a small bond dimension cannot reproduce.\n"
msgstr "Reja mengukur sejauh mana tetingkap model daripada bayang latihan. Ia menurun apabila kemas kini satu tapak bermula, pada sapuan kedua, dan kemudian kekal hampir malar dan tidak mencapai sifar, kerana bayang mengandungi noise statistik yang tidak dapat dihasilkan semula oleh model dengan dimensi ikatan kecil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because this state is known, you can compare the learned model with it exactly, and also compare the two simplest guesses with it: the CRM prior and the ideal state.\n"
msgstr "Oleh sebab keadaan ini diketahui, anda boleh membandingkan model yang dipelajari dengannya secara tepat, dan juga membandingkan dua tekaan paling ringkas dengannya: prior CRM dan keadaan unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learned model is closer to the noisy state than either the prior or the ideal state, so it has learned the noise from the data. Its small negative eigenvalues come from the finite number of measurements.\n"
msgstr "Model yang dipelajari lebih dekat dengan keadaan bernoise berbanding prior atau keadaan unggul, jadi ia telah mempelajari noise daripada data. Nilai eigen negatifnya yang kecil datang daripada bilangan pengukuran yang terhad.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, the state is unknown, so you estimate $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ from the testing settings instead. AFC splits the chain into blocks $A_1,\\dots,A_R$ of $k$ qubits and approximates the purity by\n"
msgstr "Pada perkakasan, keadaan tidak diketahui, jadi anda menganggar $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ daripada tetapan ujian. AFC membahagikan rantaian kepada blok $A_1,\\dots,A_R$ yang masing-masing $k$ qubit dan menghampiri ketulenan dengan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2\\approx\\frac{\\prod_{i=1}^{R-1}\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_{A_iA_{i+1}}^2}{\\prod_{i=2}^{R-1}\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_{A_i}^2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2\\approx\\frac{\\prod_{i=1}^{R-1}\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_{A_iA_{i+1}}^2}{\\prod_{i=2}^{R-1}\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_{A_i}^2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ by the same ratio of local overlaps. With $k=4$, the two blocks cover all eight qubits and the formula is exact; with $k=2$, it relies on the factorization assumption. The jackknife error bars, which leave out one testing setting at a time, cover the statistical error of the testing data only, not the randomness of training or the AFC approximation.\n"
msgstr "dan $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ dengan nisbah pertindihan setempat yang sama. Dengan $k=4$, kedua-dua blok meliputi kesemua lapan qubit dan formula itu tepat; dengan $k=2$, ia bergantung pada andaian pemfaktoran. Bar ralat jackknife, yang mengecualikan satu tetapan ujian pada satu masa, hanya meliputi ralat statistik data ujian, bukan kerawakan latihan atau penghampiran AFC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both held-out estimates agree with the exact value within their error bars.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua anggaran yang ditahan sepadan dengan nilai tepat dalam bar ralat masing-masing.\n"

