msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-1}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A chain is only as good as its worst qubit, so choose the 96 physical qubits yourself. The `transpile` function of `Qiskit.jl` cannot yet accept a fixed initial layout, and in a test on `ibm_phoenix`, the layout it chose included a qubit with 51% readout error. The following chain is the 96-qubit path in the `ibm_fez` coupling map that the error-aware layout of the Python Qiskit `transpile` function (with `optimization_level=3`) selected from the calibration data of 27 September 2026. Its mean readout error is 1.6%, but a heavy-hex lattice has few 96-qubit paths, and this one includes qubit 35, which has a 15% readout error. Calibrations change, so choose a new chain from the current [calibration data](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) before you run on another day or QPU.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah rantai hanya sebaik qubit yang paling lemah, jadi pilih sendiri 96 qubit fizikal. Fungsi `transpile` bagi `Qiskit.jl` belum boleh menerima susun atur awal yang tetap, dan dalam ujian pada `ibm_phoenix`, susun atur yang dipilihnya termasuk sebuah qubit dengan ralat bacaan 51%. Rantai berikut ialah laluan 96 qubit dalam peta gandingan `ibm_fez` yang dipilih oleh susun atur sedar-ralat bagi fungsi `transpile` Qiskit Python (dengan `optimization_level=3`) daripada data penentukuran pada 27 September 2026. Min ralat bacaannya ialah 1.6%, tetapi kekisi heavy-hex mempunyai sedikit laluan 96 qubit, dan laluan ini termasuk qubit 35, yang mempunyai ralat bacaan 15%. Penentukuran berubah, jadi pilih rantai baharu daripada [data penentukuran](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) semasa sebelum anda menjalankan pada hari atau QPU lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep this chain, write the circuits directly in native gates instead of transpiling them. A $U(\\theta,\\phi,\\lambda)$ gate equals $R_Z(\\phi+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\theta+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\lambda)$ up to a global phase. This decomposition covers both the random rotations and the kick $e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X}=U(\\pi/4,-\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$. The gate $e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}$ equals a CZ gate followed by $S^\\dagger$ on both qubits, up to a global phase. Because these $S^\\dagger$ gates are diagonal, they commute with the CZ gates, so each qubit collects one $R_Z(-\\pi/2)$ per bond before its measurement rotation.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengekalkan rantai ini, tulis litar terus dalam gate asli dan bukannya mentranspilnya. Sebuah gate $U(\\theta,\\phi,\\lambda)$ sama dengan $R_Z(\\phi+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\theta+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\lambda)$ sehingga fasa global. Penguraian ini merangkumi putaran rawak dan tendangan $e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X}=U(\\pi/4,-\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$. Gate $e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}$ sama dengan gate CZ diikuti $S^\\dagger$ pada kedua-dua qubit, sehingga fasa global. Oleh sebab gate $S^\\dagger$ ini bersifat pepenjuru, ia kalis tukar tertib dengan gate CZ, jadi setiap qubit mengumpul satu $R_Z(-\\pi/2)$ bagi setiap ikatan sebelum putaran pengukurannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-1}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` runs one circuit per Sampler job, so collecting the data requires 1,024 jobs. The following cell keeps up to 32 jobs in the queue and saves the outcomes of each setting as soon as its job finishes. Each shot is returned as a vector of bits, in which element $i$ is the outcome of chain qubit $i$.\n"
msgstr "`QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` menjalankan satu litar bagi setiap job Sampler, jadi pengumpulan data memerlukan 1,024 job. Sel berikut mengekalkan sehingga 32 job dalam giliran dan menyimpan hasil bagi setiap tetapan sebaik sahaja job-nya selesai. Setiap tembakan dikembalikan sebagai vektor bit, dengan elemen $i$ ialah hasil bagi qubit rantai $i$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You must retrieve the results in the same session that submitted the jobs, because `QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` cannot yet look up a job by its ID ([qiskit-ibm-runtime-c issue #28](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime-c/issues/28)). If a job fails, the cell issues a warning and continues. If the session stops, run Steps 1 through 3 again. Rerunning the cell submits only the settings whose outcomes are missing. With `use_saved_data = true`, the cell submits nothing.\n"
msgstr "Anda mesti mendapatkan semula keputusan dalam sesi yang sama yang menghantar job, kerana `QiskitIBMRuntime.jl` belum boleh mencari job melalui ID-nya ([qiskit-ibm-runtime-c issue #28](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime-c/issues/28)). Jika sesuatu job gagal, sel mengeluarkan amaran dan diteruskan. Jika sesi berhenti, jalankan semula Langkah 1 hingga 3. Menjalankan semula sel hanya menghantar tetapan yang hasilnya tiada. Dengan `use_saved_data = true`, sel tidak menghantar apa-apa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format-1}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan keputusan dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This step reads only saved data: the downloaded `ibm_fez` run if `use_saved_data` is true, or otherwise the files that Step 3 wrote. You can therefore run it in a new session without submitting jobs (run the Setup cell, the `use_saved_data` cell, and Step 1 first). The downloaded file stores the 96 outcomes of each shot packed into 12 bytes, most significant bit first, so the loader unpacks them. `RandomMeas.jl` labels outcomes 1 and 2, so the loader also adds 1 to every bit.\n"
msgstr "Langkah ini hanya membaca data tersimpan: larian `ibm_fez` yang dimuat turun jika `use_saved_data` benar, atau jika tidak, fail yang ditulis oleh Langkah 3. Oleh itu, anda boleh menjalankannya dalam sesi baharu tanpa menghantar job (jalankan sel Setup, sel `use_saved_data`, dan Langkah 1 dahulu). Fail yang dimuat turun menyimpan 96 hasil bagi setiap tembakan yang dipadatkan dalam 12 bait, bit paling bererti dahulu, jadi pemuat menyahpadatkannya. `RandomMeas.jl` melabelkan hasil 1 dan 2, jadi pemuat juga menambah 1 pada setiap bit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before learning, check the data. A broken qubit or a badly calibrated gate makes the measured state much more mixed around it, and it can make the learner diverge. The purity of a few neighboring qubits is a model-free benchmark of this noise: the function `get_purity` from `RandomMeas.jl` estimates $\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_A^2$ for a subsystem $A$ by comparing pairs of shots from the same setting. Compute the Rényi-2 entropy $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_A^2$ of every window of six neighboring qubits, and compare it with the same window of the ideal state. The ideal value is not zero, because each window is entangled with the rest of the chain; noise increases it, and a broken qubit pushes every window that contains it toward the maximum of six.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum mempelajari, semak data. Qubit yang rosak atau gate yang ditentukur dengan buruk menjadikan keadaan terukur jauh lebih bercampur di sekelilingnya, dan boleh menyebabkan pembelajar menyimpang. Ketulenan beberapa qubit berjiran ialah penanda aras bebas-model bagi hingar ini: fungsi `get_purity` daripada `RandomMeas.jl` menganggar $\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_A^2$ bagi subsistem $A$ dengan membandingkan pasangan tembakan daripada tetapan yang sama. Kira entropi Rényi-2 $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho_A^2$ bagi setiap tetingkap enam qubit berjiran, dan bandingkannya dengan tetingkap yang sama bagi keadaan unggul. Nilai unggul bukan sifar, kerana setiap tetingkap terjalin dengan bahagian rantai yang lain; hingar meningkatkannya, dan qubit yang rosak menolak setiap tetingkap yang mengandunginya ke arah maksimum enam.\n"

