# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every window is more mixed than the ideal state, by about half a bit to one bit, and the noisiest stretch is around chain positions 30 to 35. No window comes close to the maximum of six, so no qubit is broken, and the analysis uses the whole 96-qubit chain. If some windows had an entropy close to six, you would remove the qubit that those windows share and learn the longest part of the chain without it.\n"
msgstr "Setiap tetingkap lebih bercampur daripada keadaan unggul, kira-kira setengah bit hingga satu bit, dan bahagian paling bising berada sekitar kedudukan rantai 30 hingga 35. Tiada tetingkap yang menghampiri maksimum enam, jadi tiada qubit yang rosak, dan analisis menggunakan keseluruhan rantai 96 qubit. Jika sesetengah tetingkap mempunyai entropi hampir enam, anda akan membuang qubit yang dikongsi oleh tetingkap tersebut dan mempelajari bahagian rantai yang paling panjang tanpanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same purities determine the CRM prior. For each window, `fitted_prior` takes the ideal state and fits a local depolarizing strength so that its purity matches the purity measured in the training settings, as in the paper.\n"
msgstr "Ketulenan yang sama menentukan prior CRM. Bagi setiap tetingkap, `fitted_prior` mengambil keadaan unggul dan memadankan kekuatan depolarisasi setempat supaya ketulenannya sepadan dengan ketulenan yang diukur dalam tetapan latihan, seperti dalam kertas kerja itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `learn_and_validate` function in the following cell performs the rest of the analysis. It learns the model from the training settings, then estimates $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ on the testing settings for the first $N$ qubits of the chain, in steps of 12. These are the quantities in Figure 1(c,d) of the paper. The ideal state is evaluated on the same testing data as a baseline.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi `learn_and_validate` dalam sel berikut melakukan baki analisis. Ia mempelajari model daripada tetapan latihan, kemudian menganggar $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ dan $S_2$ pada tetapan ujian bagi $N$ qubit pertama rantai, dalam langkah 12. Ini ialah kuantiti dalam Rajah 1(c,d) kertas kerja itu. Keadaan unggul dinilai pada data ujian yang sama sebagai garis asas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cell runs the function with $\\ell=2$ and then repeats it with $\\ell=1$ and $\\ell=0$ to see how much the size of the learning windows matters. The bond dimension can be at most $4^\\ell$, so $\\ell=0$ learns a product state: each qubit on its own, with no correlations between qubits.\n"
msgstr "Sel menjalankan fungsi dengan $\\ell=2$ dan kemudian mengulanginya dengan $\\ell=1$ dan $\\ell=0$ untuk melihat sejauh mana saiz tetingkap pembelajaran penting. Dimensi ikatan paling banyak $4^\\ell$, jadi $\\ell=0$ mempelajari keadaan hasil darab: setiap qubit bersendirian, tanpa korelasi antara qubit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/classical-shadows/extracted-outputs/7b1b7337-2.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/classical-shadows/extracted-outputs/7b1b7337-2.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The results reproduce both claims of the paper on a different processor:\n"
msgstr "Keputusan menghasilkan semula kedua-dua dakwaan kertas kerja itu pada pemproses yang berbeza:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The model describes the data far better than the ideal state.** At $N=96$, the held-out $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ of the $\\ell=2$ model is 0.59 ± 0.10, compared with 0.0035 for the ideal state. The paper reports about 0.75 on `ibm_brisbane`.\n"
msgstr "**Model menerangkan data jauh lebih baik daripada keadaan unggul.** Pada $N=96$, $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ tertahan bagi model $\\ell=2$ ialah 0.59 ± 0.10, berbanding 0.0035 bagi keadaan unggul. Kertas kerja itu melaporkan kira-kira 0.75 pada `ibm_brisbane`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The entropy of the model agrees with the testing data at every $N$.** At $N=96$, it is 10.2 from the model and 10.0 ± 0.3 from the testing data, or $S_2/N\\approx 0.10$, compared with 0.14 to 0.15 on the older `ibm_brisbane`.\n"
msgstr "**Entropi model sepadan dengan data ujian pada setiap $N$.** Pada $N=96$, ia ialah 10.2 daripada model dan 10.0 ± 0.3 daripada data ujian, atau $S_2/N\\approx 0.10$, berbanding 0.14 hingga 0.15 pada `ibm_brisbane` yang lebih lama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The comparison of window sizes shows where the information is. With $\\ell=1$, the model is almost as good ($\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}=0.55\\pm0.09$), so for these data, correlations beyond a few qubits add little. With $\\ell=0$, the product state misses the entanglement between neighboring qubits: its entropy grows to 32 instead of 10, and its $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ falls even faster than that of the ideal state, to $6\\times10^{-6}$ at $N=96$.\n"
msgstr "Perbandingan saiz tetingkap menunjukkan di mana maklumat berada. Dengan $\\ell=1$, model hampir sebaik itu ($\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}=0.55\\pm0.09$), jadi bagi data ini, korelasi melangkaui beberapa qubit menambah sedikit sahaja. Dengan $\\ell=0$, keadaan hasil darab terlepas keterjalinan antara qubit berjiran: entropinya meningkat kepada 32 dan bukannya 10, dan $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$-nya jatuh lebih cepat lagi daripada keadaan unggul, kepada $6\\times10^{-6}$ pada $N=96$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following limitations in mind when you read these numbers:\n"
msgstr "Ingat batasan berikut apabila anda membaca nombor ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Training split.** The error bars cover the statistical error of the testing data only. Other random splits of the same settings give $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ between 0.49 and 0.59 at $N=96$ for $\\ell=2$.\n"
msgstr "**Pembahagian latihan.** Bar ralat hanya meliputi ralat statistik data ujian. Pembahagian rawak lain bagi tetapan yang sama memberikan $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ antara 0.49 dan 0.59 pada $N=96$ bagi $\\ell=2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Final sweep.** The learner always returns the model from the final sweep, so the testing data never influence the model.\n"
msgstr "**Sapuan akhir.** Pembelajar sentiasa mengembalikan model daripada sapuan akhir, jadi data ujian tidak pernah mempengaruhi model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Positivity.** The model is not constrained to be positive semidefinite; its most negative eigenvalue in a learning window is about $-0.05$. Its $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ therefore describe an operator, not certified properties of a physical state.\n"
msgstr "**Kepositifan.** Model tidak dikekang supaya positif separa tentu; nilai eigen paling negatifnya dalam tetingkap pembelajaran kira-kira $-0.05$. Oleh itu, $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ dan $S_2$-nya menerangkan sebuah pengendali, bukan sifat tersahih bagi keadaan fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Factorization.** Every held-out estimate relies on the AFC assumption, which the measurements themselves cannot certify.\n"
msgstr "**Pemfaktoran.** Setiap anggaran tertahan bergantung pada andaian AFC, yang tidak dapat disahkan oleh pengukuran itu sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah seterusnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Cadangan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the experiment at depth two with the paper's parameters for that depth ($\\ell=3$ and a maximum bond dimension of 8), and determine how many measurement settings the learner needs.\n"
msgstr "Ulang eksperimen pada kedalaman dua dengan parameter kertas kerja itu bagi kedalaman tersebut ($\\ell=3$ dan dimensi ikatan maksimum 8), dan tentukan berapa banyak tetapan pengukuran yang diperlukan oleh pembelajar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn with the two-site update instead (`update=:two_site` in `training_marginals` and `learn_mpo`), which truncates the bond dimension after every step, and see how it behaves with fewer training settings.\n"
msgstr "Belajar dengan kemas kini dua-tapak sebagai ganti (`update=:two_site` dalam `training_marginals` dan `learn_mpo`), yang memangkas dimensi ikatan selepas setiap langkah, dan lihat bagaimana ia berfungsi dengan tetapan latihan yang lebih sedikit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn without the CRM prior (`prior=nothing`) and compare the held-out fidelity.\n"
msgstr "Belajar tanpa prior CRM (`prior=nothing`) dan bandingkan kesetiaan tertahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the same analysis to the authors' published [`ibm_brisbane` measurements](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18323569).\n"
msgstr "Gunakan analisis yang sama pada [pengukuran `ibm_brisbane`](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18323569) yang diterbitkan oleh pengarang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the [supplement of the paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.12550) for the derivation of the update and of the AFC estimators.\n"
msgstr "Baca [suplemen kertas kerja itu](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.12550) untuk terbitan kemas kini dan penganggar AFC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explore other randomized-measurement protocols in the [`RandomMeas.jl` examples](https://github.com/bvermersch/RandomMeas.jl/tree/main/examples).\n"
msgstr "Terokai protokol pengukuran rawak yang lain dalam [contoh `RandomMeas.jl`](https://github.com/bvermersch/RandomMeas.jl/tree/main/examples).\n"

